From: Mohamed Ashry <contact@atharapp.download>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 06:37:48 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] docs(readme): correct crate consumers and list all 26
 pipeline modules

warsha-git claimed the pipeline asks it to prepare worktrees and open PRs.
warsha-pipeline has no dependency on it: only warshad does, and it builds a
GitHubClient into DaemonState.github at start-up and never reads the field.
Record that, name reqwest as the HTTP client (octocrab is a declared but unused
workspace dependency), and replace the false "a path outside the project is
rejected" invariant with what the code actually refuses.

templates claimed the directory is empty and find returns nothing. It holds this
README; the four scaffolds are embedded in warsha-git as ProjectTemplate and
nothing outside that crate calls them.

warsha-pipeline listed 11 of its modules. List all 26 declared at lib.rs:18-50
(23 private, 3 public) one line each from the module's own header doc, plus the
cfg(test) test_util. Correct "nine-stage" to the 14 Stage variants and the
claim that caches live under the daemon data directory: both implementations
are in-memory and the traits are the persistence seam.
